1
00:00:03,881 --> 00:00:04,894
Hi everyone!

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:07,641
Today, I'll explain
the "hand on the floor" trick.

3
00:00:07,894 --> 00:00:10,101
There are several variations
of this trick,

4
00:00:10,207 --> 00:00:12,507
but the first one I learned

5
00:00:12,772 --> 00:00:17,393
starts from a "seat on side idle"

6
00:00:17,763 --> 00:00:21,780
with the frame behind your legs.

7
00:00:21,846 --> 00:00:33,152
[Music]

8
00:00:33,218 --> 00:00:36,607
For this "idle", I first learned
to start it from the ground,

9
00:00:36,851 --> 00:00:40,715
with one foot on the pedal
and the other one passing in front,

10
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:44,990
and then I tried to hold the "idle".

11
00:00:45,056 --> 00:00:53,058
[Music]

12
00:00:53,171 --> 00:00:59,218
Once you've mastered the "idle",
move on to the "hand on the floor",

13
00:00:59,584 --> 00:01:04,098
which means putting your hand
down next to you.

14
00:01:04,150 --> 00:01:06,384
There are several things to watch out for.

15
00:01:06,471 --> 00:01:09,711
Don't put your hand on the floor
too far away,

16
00:01:09,770 --> 00:01:14,378
or you'll be at a bad angle
and the unicycle tends to slide.

17
00:01:14,871 --> 00:01:18,884
Don't put your hand down too close,
or you'll be all cramped

18
00:01:18,950 --> 00:01:21,585
and have trouble turning around your hand.

19
00:01:21,831 --> 00:01:24,631
Also, as you go around in a circle,

20
00:01:24,883 --> 00:01:30,191
don't let the wheel drift away,
because then it tends to slide too.

21
00:01:30,297 --> 00:01:32,890
So try to ride a proper circle.

22
00:01:37,051 --> 00:01:41,865
Try to keep the unicycle upright,

23
00:01:43,731 --> 00:01:46,012
parallel to your hand,

24
00:01:46,358 --> 00:01:47,691
or rather your arm on the ground,

25
00:01:47,897 --> 00:01:52,178
because if it leans to one side
or the other, it gets tricky.

26
00:01:52,344 --> 00:01:55,991
Once you're in the right position,
try turning.

27
00:01:56,277 --> 00:02:01,130
And as you turn, don't forget
to shift your hand every now and then.

28
00:02:01,196 --> 00:02:10,921
[Music]

29
00:02:11,007 --> 00:02:13,868
Your weight is on the hand

30
00:02:13,968 --> 00:02:20,174
on the ground, so to get back up,
shift more weight

31
00:02:20,307 --> 00:02:21,767
onto the unicycle.

32
00:02:23,801 --> 00:02:27,574
You feel the weight
shift onto the wheel,

33
00:02:27,873 --> 00:02:33,000
and then you can push yourself
back up.

34
00:02:35,107 --> 00:02:37,361
Also, when you try
the "hand on the floor",

35
00:02:37,487 --> 00:02:39,568
think about the position of the hand
that holds the unicycle.

36
00:02:39,847 --> 00:02:41,754
Personally, what works best for me

37
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:46,248
is to put my hand, or rather,
grip the saddle in the middle,

38
00:02:46,314 --> 00:02:49,301
right where the dip is,
but I guess you could also

39
00:02:49,633 --> 00:02:52,048
hold the saddle by the handle.

40
00:02:52,414 --> 00:02:56,348
So find a good grip,
the one that works best for you.

41
00:02:56,521 --> 00:03:00,141
As with all my advice,
it's just what works for me.

42
00:03:00,167 --> 00:03:03,381
So if something seems a bit hard,

43
00:03:03,420 --> 00:03:06,701
like starting
with the "seat on side idle",

44
00:03:07,227 --> 00:03:11,120
and you find another way that works,
that's fine too.

45
00:03:11,239 --> 00:03:36,841
[Music]

46
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,886
Finally, I didn't show this in the video,

47
00:03:39,924 --> 00:03:43,635
but once you can turn forward,
you can turn backward too,

48
00:03:43,739 --> 00:03:46,299
and there's also

49
00:03:47,172 --> 00:03:50,241
the "drag seat in front",
forward and backward.

50
00:03:50,513 --> 00:03:55,134
I hope my tips were helpful,
and good luck.

51
00:03:55,545 --> 00:03:56,681
Now it's your turn to try.

52
00:03:56,814 --> 00:04:01,100
This trick looks harder
than it actually is.

